## Lesson: check-splitting-before-cech
Lesson ID: BL-20261003-check-splitting-before-cech
Scope: category/topos cohomology endgames (proving a unit
  obj -> R lower-star upper-star obj is an isomorphism for ALL
  presheaves/sheaves), e.g. solution.tex Section 4 (prop:vanish).
Problem Description: Attempting to push a Cech/descent argument
  through to prove a unit map is a quasi-isomorphism for all
  presheaves F, only to discover late that the claim is false or
  unprovable in that generality: the endgame "almost works" at
  degree 0 (descent) and on constant/nice pieces, so the failure is
  not triggered until the derived/higher-degree or non-cover cases.
Root Cause: The unit factors through a change-of-site/categorical
  adjunction whose derived functors split: obj ≅ r_*r⁻¹obj ⊕ (derived
  complement). The complement (e.g. R pi_* M, M the part living off the
  sub-site) is generally nonzero, and descent (a degree-0 statement)
  plus a sieve/support filtration says nothing about it. The only way
  the unit is an iso for all F is if the inverse image always lands in
  sheaves concentrated on the sub-site, a concentration/sheaf property
  that is the real content and is independent of the descent step.
Solution: Before investing in the Cech endgame, factor the unit
  through the change-of-site derived functors and TEST the claim on
  idempotent/atomic presheaves (constant value A, zero transitions).
  These are the cheapest witnesses and immediately expose the
  complement term. If the claim survives only under a
  "inverse-image-is-concentrated-on-the-sub-site" hypothesis, prove or
  refute THAT hypothesis directly (it is the crux), or build the
  explicit counterexample and report via AC-4 rather than fabricating
  the filtration step.
Constraints: Applies when the goal is a for-all-presheaves statement;
  for a fixed F the descent + filtration route may still be fine.
Validation Evidence: prob-001 Round 2: the derived-fiber/splitting
  analysis (B_P as a finite poset = inverse system; idempotent F) made
  the complement R pi_* M explicit and showed Steps 1-3 of prop:vanish
  could not close without assuming the conclusion; recorded honestly in
  round-2-summary.md / goal-tracker.md.
